Priority: 2
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-multi-select, add-stroke-selection-editing

Goal:
Allow the current selection set to have its colors and stroke width changed directly.

Context:
The user wants to modify selected objects after creation instead of only changing the active tool defaults. This becomes especially important once multi-select exists.

Expected changes:

- controls or commands that apply color changes to the current selection
- controls or commands that apply stroke-width changes to the current selection
- batch application across supported selected items

Acceptance criteria:

- Selected objects can have color changed after they are created.
- Selected vector objects can have stroke width changed after they are created.
- Applying style changes to a mixed supported selection updates the selected objects without corrupting selection state.

Notes:

- Keep this scoped to post-selection style edits, not a full inspector panel redesign.
